  - Attacks: "+1 additional attack per melee; this is in addition to the two attacks per melee all Vrill start off with or those gained from hand to hand combat skills" (printed 67). Stored as combat.attacks 1.
  - The five radar percentages (50/60/50/40/40, +5 or +4 per level) are abilities, not catalog skills, and are stored as prose.
  - Psionics, printed 68: only a Psi-Mystic or Psi-Healer Vrill has psionics, and a Vrill of any other O.C.C. cannot. Stored as psionics_allowed false, so no Vrill rolls for random psionics and the two psychic occupations bring their own; the rule is repeated as a restrictions line.
  - Languages, printed 68: all Vrill speak, read and write Elven and Dwarven, as well as Gobblely at 98%, and can learn no other language above 10%. Elven is Language: Dragonese and Literacy: Dragonese/Elven; the 98 is read as covering all three tongues. The catalog has no Dwarven literacy row, so reading and writing Dwarven is prose on the Language: Dwarven line. The 10% ceiling on every other language is stored as prose.
  - Swimming is the natural-ability line "instinctive swimmers 90%" (printed 67), a fixed figure with no per-level gain printed.
  - O.C.C.s Available, printed 67 and repeated on printed 215 ("Vrill are limited to the following"): Monk (scholarly, not warrior monks), Scholars, Rangers, Sailors, Druids, Psi-Healers or Psi-Mystics for 95%, and "of that other 5%, most become Warlocks or Clergy". It is an allow-list, so occ_restrictions is `only`: scholar, ranger, druid, psi-healer, psi-mystic, and for Clergy priest-of-light and priest-of-darkness. warrior-monk is left out because the book excludes warrior monks by name. The scholarly Monk, the Sailor and the Warlock are named by the book and are not Palladium Fantasy occupations in the catalog; one imported later is not covered until it is added. "Most" of the last 5% leaves a remainder the book does not name; nothing is listed for it.
  - Printed 215 says Vrill use the experience table of their chosen O.C.C., so no xp_table is stated.
  - Size 5 and a half to 6 feet (1.6 to 1.8 m), 160 to 170 lbs (72 to 76.5 kg); average life span 100 years. In the Lore.
