# Vrill

## Lore

The Vrill are among the rarest peoples of the Baalgor Wastelands, and the least understood, themselves included. They arrived on the Palladium World during the Elf-Dwarf War and were all but wiped out in it. Whoever destroyed them seems to have taken their memory as well: no Vrill knows where the race came from, why it was brought here or how it was undone, and that missing past is an ache every one of them carries. Scholars guess that they came to destroy rune weapons, or as peacemakers or healers, or simply by accident.

A Vrill is a slender, upright reptilian with a good deal of the amphibian about it: rough tan scales, oversized eyes with a protective inner lid, hands and feet with few digits, a low finned crest down the length of the spine, and a broad mouth full of little teeth. They are lithe rather than strong.

They are a gentle, curious, open-minded people who value life, argue for peace and wander to learn about the world and, with luck, about themselves. Most are healers, explorers and mystics, travelling alone, in pairs or with any band of adventurers that will have them. They settle only to raise children, own little, and carry less.

**Alignment:** Any, but they lean toward good or selfish.

**O.C.C.s available:** Scholarly Monk, Scholar, Ranger, Sailor, Druid, Psi-Healer or Psi-Mystic for nearly all; a few become Warlocks or Clergy.

**Size:** 5 and a half to 6 feet tall (1.6 to 1.8 m). **Weight:** 160 to 170 lbs (72 to 76.5 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 100 years.

**Habitat:** Mostly the Baalgor Wastelands, where they first appeared and are not hunted. Also reported in the Old Kingdom around Mount Nimro and in the emptier parts of Timiro and the southern Eastern Territory. They dislike very wet climates and handle cold poorly.

**Languages:** Elven and Dwarven, spoken, read and written, and Gobblely. They have no tongue of their own and cannot master any other.

## GM Notes

"Civilized" humans tend to take a Vrill for a monster and attack on sight, which is why the race keeps to the Wastelands; a slowly spreading name as healers and sages is beginning to change that. The Vrill hold no grudge and count no people as an enemy, not even the humans and ogres who have hunted them. Dragonmen, Eandroth, Gosai, Quorians, Quillbacks and many orc and goblin tribes treat them as friends, and the orc and goblin tribes take them in as honored healers.

The radar bonuses are stored as always on. In rain, snow, dust or a sandstorm they are gone entirely, extra attack included, and in smoke they are halved; in a desert campaign that will come up, and it has to be applied by hand.

A Vrill family raises its surviving young for three years and then parts; siblings travel together for another 1D4 years. A child may be named for a dead brother or sister as a "ghost" sibling.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'vrill');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'vrill';

